{
 "section_summary": "This section finishes an analysis of Japan’s postwar left, tracing the fall of the Katayama cabinet, the formation and collapse of the Ashida cabinet, disputes within the Socialist Party, and competing Communist and anti-Communist campaigns in labor organizations. Its conclusions assess the Socialists’ record in government and the prospects for the divided left in 1949. The section then begins an appendix of biographical notes on Japanese left-wing leaders.",
